{"id":"shikoku-henro","title":"Shikoku 88 Temple Pilgrimage","who":"Classic route · Japan's henro circuit","when":"March–May and October–November","vehicle":"On foot, 5–8 weeks (or by bike, bus or car)","kind":"walk","color":"#be123c","summary":"A loop of about 1,200 km round the island of Shikoku visiting 88 temples linked to the monk Kūkai, walked in white clothes with a sedge hat and staff. Coast roads, mountain temples, Cape Muroto and Cape Ashizuri, and the custom of osettai: gifts from locals to pilgrims. About 25 km a day.","sources":[{"label":"Notes from a Dadbear: day 56, temples 87 and 88 (June 2025)","url":"https://buttondown.com/cpratt/archive/day-56-t87-t88-from-takamatsu"},{"label":"Treeline Review: Shikoku 88 Temple Pilgrimage guide","url":"https://www.treelinereview.com/where-to-go/shikoku-88-temple-pilgrimage"}],"approximate":"Key temples and towns; the line follows roads near the pilgrim route.","km":968,"bbox":[132.5608,32.7239,134.5028,34.2721],"stops":[{"name":"Temple 1: Ryōzen-ji","place":"Ryōzen-ji, Naruto","at":[34.1594,134.5028],"text":"Most henro start here, buying their white clothes and stamp book."},{"name":"Temple 12: Shōsan-ji","place":"Shōsan-ji, Kamiyama","at":[33.9851,134.3104],"text":"The \"henro korogashi\", the first steep mountain temple."},{"name":"Cape Muroto","place":"Cape Muroto","at":[33.2436,134.1768],"text":"A long coast walk to the cape where Kūkai is said to have found enlightenment.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Muroto_Cape.JPG/500px-Muroto_Cape.JPG","page":"Cape Muroto","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muroto_Cape.JPG","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Kōchi","place":"Kōchi, Japan","at":[33.6569,133.5606],"text":"Kōchi's castle and Sunday market.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Kochi_Castle_2025.jpg/500px-Kochi_Castle_2025.jpg","page":"Kōchi Castle","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kochi_Castle_2025.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Cape Ashizuri","place":"Cape Ashizuri","at":[32.7235,133.0201],"text":"The southern tip, temple 38 among camellias."},{"name":"Uwajima","place":"Uwajima, Japan","at":[33.2232,132.5607],"text":"Into Ehime prefecture.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Uwajima_Bay.JPG/500px-Uwajima_Bay.JPG","page":"Uwajima","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uwajima_Bay.JPG","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Matsuyama","place":"Matsuyama, Japan","at":[33.8395,132.7654],"text":"Dōgo Onsen, one of Japan's oldest hot springs.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Dogo_onsen_honkan_long_exposure.jpg/500px-Dogo_onsen_honkan_long_exposure.jpg","page":"Dōgo Onsen","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dogo_onsen_honkan_long_exposure.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Temple 66: Unpen-ji","place":"Unpen-ji","at":[34.0351,133.7229],"text":"The highest temple, about 900 m.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Unpenji20211106_1.jpg/500px-Unpenji20211106_1.jpg","page":"Unpen-ji","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unpenji20211106_1.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Temple 88: Ōkubo-ji","place":"Ōkubo-ji","at":[34.1914,134.2069],"text":"The last temple, where pilgrims leave their staffs.","source":{"label":"Notes from a Dadbear (2025)","url":"https://buttondown.com/cpratt/archive/day-56-t87-t88-from-takamatsu"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Iozan-okuboji-main.JPG/500px-Iozan-okuboji-main.JPG","page":"Ōkubo-ji","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iozan-okuboji-main.JPG","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}}],"legs":[{"by":"walk","km":35,"line":[[34.1593,134.5028],[34.14